# UPGRADE-22
# Durable Autonomous Engineering Fleet
# & Multi-Repository Portfolio Management
#
# P0:
# Complete Upgrade-21 durability proof with
# real process crashes, real PostgreSQL concurrency,
# real Git/worktree/commit reconciliation,
# and durable external-operation journal.
#
# THEN:
# Multi-repository task fleet,
# portfolio scheduling,
# repository health,
# maintenance campaigns,
# dependency/security campaigns,
# fleet capacity,
# cross-repository coordination,
# durable campaign execution,
# and portfolio observability.
#
# PRIMARY PRINCIPLES
#
# NO-COST FIRST
# LOCAL-FIRST
# REAL DURABILITY BEFORE SCALE
# DATABASE-BACKED COORDINATION
# NO REDIS/KAFKA REQUIRED
# NO SILENT PAID FALLBACK
# NO SILENT REPOSITORY MUTATION
# NO SILENT PUSH/MERGE
# FAIRNESS BETWEEN REPOSITORIES
# SECURITY/QUALITY OVERRIDE THROUGHPUT
# EVERY EXTERNAL MUTATION MUST BE RECONCILABLE

You are operating directly inside ZCoder after Upgrade-21.

================================================================
MISSION
================================================================

Upgrade-21 reportedly introduced:

engineering_models.py
engineering_store_interface.py
SQLiteEngineeringStore
PostgresEngineeringStore
EngineeringOrchestrator

with durable:

EngineeringTask
Attempt
Checkpoint

However, the reported verification currently proves primarily:

- SQLite task/attempt/checkpoint persistence
- simulated restart behavior
- store/orchestrator integration

Before scaling to a fleet, Upgrade-22 MUST prove the durability
properties required for distributed execution.

After those gates pass, build:

Repository Portfolio
        │
        ▼
Engineering Campaign
        │
        ▼
Portfolio Scheduler
        │
        ├── Repo A Queue
        ├── Repo B Queue
        ├── Repo C Queue
        └── ...
              │
              ▼
        Fleet Workers
              │
      ┌───────┼─────────┐
      ▼       ▼         ▼
   Worker A Worker B  Worker C
      │       │         │
      └───────┼─────────┘
              ▼
      Durable Engineering Store
              │
              ├── tasks
              ├── attempts
              ├── checkpoints
              ├── leases
              ├── operations
              ├── campaigns
              └── repo health
              │
              ▼
      Local Model Runtime Fleet

The system must support many repositories and many durable autonomous
tasks without duplicate execution, starvation, uncontrolled mutation,
or commercial infrastructure requirements.

