================================================================
P0.1 — REAL PROCESS RESTART
================================================================

Upgrade-21 report says:

"simulated process restarts"

This is not sufficient for HARD_CRASH_RECOVERY.

Create an actual subprocess test.

Process A:

open SQLite store
create task
create attempt
create checkpoints
flush/commit

then terminate process.

Process B:

fresh Python interpreter
open same SQLite file
load task
attempt
checkpoint

Verify:

same IDs
same state
same sequence
same attempt history

No shared Python memory.

================================================================
P0.2 — HARD CRASH
================================================================

Test abrupt termination.

Use controlled fault-injection subprocess.

Crash points:

after task persistence
after attempt persistence
after checkpoint
after edit metadata
after validation metadata

Do not rely only on graceful close.

================================================================
P0.3 — SQLITE CRASH SAFETY
================================================================

Use actual SQLite file.

Verify transaction boundaries.

A partially written transition must not create impossible state.

Inspect use of:

transactions
foreign keys
journaling/WAL

Document actual decision.

================================================================
P0.4 — POSTGRESQL REAL INTEGRATION
================================================================

PostgresEngineeringStore must not be called verified solely because
class exists.

Run against actual PostgreSQL.

No fake cursor/database.

Verify:

schema
CRUD
tenant scoping
transactions
claims
leases
checkpoints

================================================================
P0.5 — POSTGRESQL RLS
================================================================

Any tenant-owned engineering tables require real database policies.

Verify using non-superuser application role:

Org A cannot:

SELECT
INSERT
UPDATE
DELETE

Org B rows.

================================================================
P0.6 — MULTI-PROCESS CLAIM
================================================================

Launch at least 3 independent worker processes.

Create multiple runnable engineering tasks.

Workers contend simultaneously.

Expected:

each task claimed once
duplicate execution = 0

Persist worker/lease evidence.

================================================================
P0.7 — STALE WORKER FENCING
================================================================

Worker A claims task.

Lose/expire lease.

Worker B claims newer generation.

A attempts mutation afterward.

Expected:

rejected.

Test DB mutation and external-operation precondition.

================================================================
P0.8 — REAL GIT REPOSITORY
================================================================

Create actual temporary repository using git CLI.

No fake git abstraction.

Record:

git version
baseline SHA
branch

================================================================
P0.9 — REAL GIT WORKTREE
================================================================

Run actual git worktree creation.

Verify:

actual .git/worktree registration
actual branch
actual base SHA
primary workspace unchanged

================================================================
P0.10 — WORKTREE RESTART RECONCILIATION
================================================================

Process A:

create actual worktree
persist registry
crash

Process B:

load durable state
run git worktree list
reconcile existing worktree

Expected:

no duplicate worktree
no lost task

================================================================
P0.11 — REAL EDIT
================================================================

Modify actual source file inside actual worktree.

Verify primary repository remains unchanged.

================================================================
P0.12 — REAL VALIDATION
================================================================

Create controlled failing project.

Baseline:

pytest fails

Patch:

actual source edit

Final:

pytest succeeds

Record actual subprocess output/exit state.

================================================================
P0.13 — REAL COMMIT
================================================================

Create actual Git commit.

Persist actual SHA.

No synthetic commit object.

================================================================
P0.14 — COMMIT CRASH WINDOW
================================================================

Critical test:

git commit succeeds
process crashes before EngineeringStore records success

Fresh process restarts.

Reconcile:

worktree HEAD
parent
tree
operation journal

Expected:

detect existing commit
do not create duplicate commit

================================================================
P0.15 — DURABLE OPERATION JOURNAL
================================================================

Create:

EngineeringOperation

Operations:

COMMIT
PUSH
CREATE_PR
UPDATE_PR
MERGE
CI_REPAIR_PUSH

Fields:

operation_id
task_id
attempt_id
operation_type
target
payload_fingerprint
state
created_at
started_at
completed_at
result_reference
error
generation/fence

States:

PLANNED
STARTED
SUCCEEDED
FAILED
UNKNOWN
RECONCILING

================================================================
P0.16 — UNKNOWN IS FIRST-CLASS
================================================================

If process/network dies after side effect may have happened:

state = UNKNOWN

Never:

UNKNOWN
→ blindly execute same mutation

Instead:

UNKNOWN
→ RECONCILING
→ SUCCEEDED / RETRYABLE_FAILED

================================================================
P0.17 — REAL LOCAL REMOTE
================================================================

Create local bare Git repository.

Use it as actual remote.

Push actual branch.

Verify remote ref.

No GitHub needed.

================================================================
P0.18 — PUSH CRASH WINDOW
================================================================

Remote accepts push.

Process dies before durable success write.

Restart.

Inspect remote ref.

Mark operation SUCCEEDED.

Do not push divergent duplicate.

================================================================
P0.19 — APPROVAL DURABILITY
================================================================

Persist approvals.

Restart.

Verify approval remains bound to:

task
attempt
operation
payload hash
policy version
expiry

================================================================
P0.20 — UPGRADE-21 DURABILITY GATE
================================================================

Do not proceed to fleet implementation unless at minimum:

SQLITE_DURABILITY = PASS
PROCESS_RESTART_RECOVERY = PASS
HARD_CRASH_RECOVERY = PASS
REAL_GIT_REPOSITORY = PASS
REAL_GIT_WORKTREE = PASS
REAL_VALIDATION = PASS
REAL_COMMIT = PASS
OPERATION_JOURNAL = PASS
COMMIT_RECONCILIATION = PASS
LOCAL_REMOTE_PUSH = PASS

PostgreSQL may be separately environment-dependent, but if
distributed/multi-worker claims are made, PostgreSQL tests become
required.

================================================================
PART 2 — REPOSITORY PORTFOLIO MODEL
================================================================

Create:

RepositoryPortfolio

A portfolio is a collection of repositories managed by an organization
or local operator.

Fields conceptually:

id
organization_id
name
description
policy_profile
default_cost_policy
created_at

================================================================
22. REPOSITORY RESOURCE
================================================================

Create/consolidate:

ManagedRepository

Fields:

id
portfolio_id
organization_id
project_id optional
name
local_path
remote_provider
remote_reference
default_branch
status
health
policy_profile
last_scan_at

================================================================
23. REPOSITORY STATUS
================================================================

States:

DISCOVERED
ACTIVE
DEGRADED
PAUSED
DISABLED
ARCHIVED

Do not delete repository history just because it becomes inactive.

================================================================
24. REPOSITORY SOURCE TYPES
================================================================

Support:

LOCAL_GIT
GITHUB
future provider

Core operation must support LOCAL_GIT.

GitHub remains optional.

================================================================
25. PORTFOLIO DISCOVERY
================================================================

Allow explicit repository registration.

Do NOT scan entire home directory automatically.

Example:

zcoder portfolio add /path/repo

================================================================
26. BULK IMPORT
================================================================

Support explicit directory/root import with:

dry-run
depth limit
repository limit
ignore rules

Never recursively crawl entire filesystem without scope.

================================================================
27. GITHUB PORTFOLIO IMPORT
================================================================

Optional:

import repositories visible to configured GitHub installation.

Do not automatically enable autonomous mutation.

Imported repos begin:

DISCOVERED
or
READ_ONLY

until policy permits.

================================================================
28. REPOSITORY READINESS
================================================================

Reuse ProjectBootstrapService.

Each ManagedRepository has readiness dimensions:

ANALYSIS_READY
VALIDATION_READY
LOCAL_AI_READY
EDIT_READY
GIT_WRITE_READY
PR_READY

================================================================
29. REPOSITORY HEALTH
================================================================

Create:

RepositoryHealthSnapshot

Signals:

bootstrap readiness
default branch
dirty/local condition
test baseline
CI state
security findings
dependency status
last autonomous run
model readiness

================================================================
30. HEALTH STATUS
================================================================

Use:

HEALTHY
DEGRADED
FAILING
UNKNOWN

Do not reduce everything to one arbitrary percentage.

================================================================
31. HEALTH EVIDENCE
================================================================

Every status references actual evidence/timestamp.

Stale data becomes STALE/UNKNOWN.

================================================================
32. ENGINEERING CAMPAIGN
================================================================

Create:

EngineeringCampaign

A campaign creates coordinated tasks across repository portfolio.

Examples:

CI_REPAIR
DEPENDENCY_UPDATE
SECURITY_PATCH
DOCUMENTATION_REFRESH
TEST_MAINTENANCE
CUSTOM

================================================================
33. CAMPAIGN IS NOT ONE GIANT AGENT
================================================================

Campaign creates bounded per-repository EngineeringTasks.

Reuse Upgrade-20/21 execution loop.

================================================================
34. CAMPAIGN STATE
================================================================

States:

DRAFT
PLANNED
RUNNING
PAUSED
COMPLETED
PARTIAL
FAILED
CANCELLED

================================================================
35. CAMPAIGN POLICY
================================================================

Campaign defines:

scope
repository selection
task template
max repositories
concurrency
cost policy
mutation policy
PR policy
approval policy
failure policy

================================================================
36. DRY RUN
================================================================

Campaign defaults to planning/dry-run where mutation is significant.

Show:

repositories targeted
tasks
expected mutations
validators
models
remote actions

================================================================
37. REPOSITORY SELECTION
================================================================

Select by explicit criteria.

Examples:

tag
language
health state
CI failure
dependency
project

Do not allow arbitrary unsafe query execution.

================================================================
38. CAMPAIGN SNAPSHOT
================================================================

Persist exact repository set selected when campaign starts.

Changing portfolio later must not silently change active campaign.

================================================================
39. CAMPAIGN TASK
================================================================

Each repository gets separate durable EngineeringTask.

No shared mutable attempt between repositories.

================================================================
40. CAMPAIGN RESUME
================================================================

Restart ZCoder.

Campaign + child task progress survives.

================================================================
41. CAMPAIGN CANCEL
================================================================

Stop new task dispatch.

Handle running tasks using cancellation policy.

================================================================
42. CAMPAIGN RETRY
================================================================

Retry failed repository tasks only.

Do not rerun already successful ones unless explicitly requested.

================================================================
43. PORTFOLIO SCHEDULER
================================================================

Create:

PortfolioScheduler

Responsibilities:

campaign task dispatch
repository fairness
worker capacity
local inference capacity
per-repository concurrency
priority
maintenance windows

================================================================
44. SCHEDULER DOES NOT EXECUTE TASK
================================================================

It dispatches durable EngineeringTasks to existing EngineeringOrchestrator.

================================================================
45. FLEET WORKER
================================================================

Create/consolidate:

EngineeringWorker

It:

claims durable task
verifies fence
loads project state
executes attempt
writes checkpoints
releases claim

================================================================
46. WORKER IDENTITY
================================================================

Persist:

worker_id
instance
host
pid
started_at
last_heartbeat
capabilities

Do not rely on PID globally.

================================================================
47. WORKER CAPABILITIES
================================================================

Examples:

LOCAL_GIT
GITHUB
CPU_LOCAL_AI
GPU_LOCAL_AI
PYTHON
NODE
DOCKER

Capabilities constrain dispatch.

================================================================
48. WORKER REGISTRATION
================================================================

Workers register durably.

Missing heartbeat eventually becomes unavailable.

================================================================
49. HEARTBEAT
================================================================

Use bounded heartbeat interval.

Do not create excessive DB write load.

================================================================
50. WORKER LEASE
================================================================

Reuse authoritative lease/fencing.

No new competing ownership system.

================================================================
51. FLEET CAPACITY
================================================================

Track:

total workers
busy
idle
queued tasks
local AI slots
RAM pressure

================================================================
52. LOCAL MODEL CAPACITY
================================================================

Integrate Upgrade-17 LocalInferenceScheduler.

Do not dispatch more local AI tasks than hardware safely supports.

================================================================
53. CPU HOST FAIRNESS
================================================================

Current known host class may be CPU-only.

Avoid queueing 20 simultaneous LLM jobs on 8 cores.

================================================================
54. REPOSITORY FAIRNESS
================================================================

One broken repo cannot consume whole fleet indefinitely.

Use bounded per-repository concurrency.

================================================================
55. ORGANIZATION FAIRNESS
================================================================

In multi-tenant mode:

prevent one organization from starving another.

================================================================
56. CAMPAIGN FAIRNESS
================================================================

Large campaign cannot block interactive engineering task indefinitely.

Priority classes:

INTERACTIVE
NORMAL
CAMPAIGN
BACKGROUND

================================================================
57. STARVATION PREVENTION
================================================================

Use aging or suitable bounded strategy.

================================================================
58. GLOBAL CONCURRENCY
================================================================

Configurable:

max_running_tasks

================================================================
59. PER-REPOSITORY CONCURRENCY
================================================================

Default conservative value.

Multiple worktrees are possible, but excessive simultaneous edits on
same repository increase conflict probability.

================================================================
60. PER-CAMPAIGN CONCURRENCY
================================================================

Campaign can have independent cap.

================================================================
61. MODEL CAPACITY AS RESOURCE
================================================================

Scheduler considers:

runtime
model
resident state
slots
RAM
quality requirements

================================================================
62. NO OVERSUBSCRIPTION
================================================================

Portfolio scheduler cannot bypass LocalInferenceScheduler admission.

================================================================
63. WORKER FAILURE
================================================================

Worker dies.

Lease expires.

Another worker resumes task from durable checkpoint.

================================================================
64. WORKER DRAIN
================================================================

Support:

DRAINING

No new tasks.

Current task may finish.

================================================================
65. WORKER DISABLE
================================================================

Operator can disable unhealthy worker.

================================================================
66. REPOSITORY LOCK
================================================================

Some operations require exclusive repository-level mutation slot.

Do not globally lock repo for read-only analysis unnecessarily.

================================================================
67. CONFLICT DOMAIN
================================================================

Track:

base branch
target branch
files likely touched

Use it as advisory scheduling evidence.

Do not claim conflict prediction is perfect.

================================================================
68. SAME-REPO TASKS
================================================================

Two isolated worktrees allowed where policies permit.

Before push/PR:

perform drift/conflict checks.

================================================================
69. CROSS-REPO DEPENDENCIES
================================================================

Create optional dependency graph.

Example:

library repo
→ service repo

Do not infer dependencies purely from repository names.

================================================================
70. DEPENDENCY SOURCE
================================================================

Evidence can come from:

package manifests
workspace config
explicit configuration
artifact references

================================================================
71. REPOSITORY GRAPH
================================================================

Represent:

RepositoryDependency

source
target
type
evidence
confidence

================================================================
72. DEPENDENCY CYCLES
================================================================

Handle safely.

Do not assume portfolio graph is DAG.

================================================================
73. DEPENDENCY-AWARE CAMPAIGN
================================================================

Example:

update shared library
→ validate dependent repos

But only if explicit/evidence-backed dependency exists.

================================================================
74. CROSS-REPO TASK GRAPH
================================================================

Support dependencies between tasks where needed.

Reuse workflow/dependency primitives.

================================================================
75. DO NOT OVERBUILD DAG ENGINE
================================================================

If existing WorkflowEngine supports it, reuse it.

================================================================
76. DEPENDENCY UPDATE CAMPAIGN
================================================================

Implement safe architecture for dependency maintenance.

Do not blindly update every dependency to latest.

================================================================
77. DEPENDENCY DETECTION
================================================================

Use ecosystem files.

Examples:

pyproject
requirements
package.json
lockfiles

================================================================
78. UPDATE POLICY
================================================================

Support:

PATCH_ONLY
MINOR_ALLOWED
EXPLICIT_VERSION
SECURITY_ONLY

================================================================
79. NO AUTO-MAJOR
================================================================

Major version updates require explicit policy/approval.

================================================================
80. LOCKFILE
================================================================

Respect native package manager.

Do not manually fabricate lockfile changes.

================================================================
81. INSTALL COMMAND
================================================================

Use detected package manager.

No silent global installs.

================================================================
82. DEPENDENCY CAMPAIGN VALIDATION
================================================================

Each repository independently:

baseline
update
tests
review

Failure does not imply every repository must stop.

================================================================
83. SECURITY CAMPAIGN
================================================================

Architecture can create security repair tasks.

Do not claim vulnerability detection completeness.

================================================================
84. SECURITY INPUT
================================================================

Potential sources:

existing scanner output
dependency advisory input
manual finding
CI result

Core should not require paid scanner.

================================================================
85. SECURITY FIX PRIORITY
================================================================

Critical/high may receive higher queue priority.

Still preserve safety/approval.

================================================================
86. CI REPAIR CAMPAIGN
================================================================

Find repositories with failing CI evidence.

Create bounded CI repair tasks.

================================================================
87. CI DISCOVERY REQUIRED
================================================================

Upgrade-21 P0 must have completed CI discovery before this campaign is
called verified.

================================================================
88. DOCUMENTATION CAMPAIGN
================================================================

Low-risk example campaign.

Can identify missing/stale docs using deterministic project signals.

Do not auto-push by default.

================================================================
89. TEST MAINTENANCE CAMPAIGN
================================================================

Examples:

fix known failing tests
modernize test configuration

Never weaken tests to make campaign green.

================================================================
90. CODE QUALITY CAMPAIGN
================================================================

Lint/type failures may be targeted.

Do not reformat entire portfolio unexpectedly.

================================================================
91. AUTONOMOUS MAINTENANCE WINDOW
================================================================

Allow campaign schedule configuration.

Core system does not require external scheduler SaaS.

================================================================
92. DURABLE CAMPAIGN SCHEDULE
================================================================

Store schedule/next run durably.

================================================================
93. MISSED RUN
================================================================

Define policy:

SKIP
RUN_ON_START
RESCHEDULE

Do not execute hundreds of missed campaigns after long downtime by
accident.

================================================================
94. PORTFOLIO BASELINE
================================================================

Create periodic repository health snapshot.

Do not continuously run expensive tests.

================================================================
95. HEALTH REFRESH
================================================================

Trigger:

manual
campaign
task
scheduled low-frequency

================================================================
96. STALE HEALTH
================================================================

Old health snapshot must display freshness.

================================================================
97. REPOSITORY RISK
================================================================

Optional risk classification:

LOW
MEDIUM
HIGH

Based on configuration.

Do not infer business criticality automatically without evidence.

================================================================
98. PROTECTED REPOSITORIES
================================================================

Allow policy:

NO_AUTONOMOUS_WRITE
APPROVAL_REQUIRED
LOCAL_ONLY
PR_ONLY

================================================================
99. REPOSITORY POLICY PRECEDENCE
================================================================

Global
→ organization
→ portfolio
→ repository
→ task

More restrictive policy wins.

================================================================
100. CAMPAIGN CANNOT OVERRIDE SECURITY
================================================================

A campaign cannot grant itself additional permissions.

================================================================
101. REMOTE MUTATION POLICY
================================================================

Portfolio-wide default:

LOCAL_ONLY

Unless explicitly changed.

================================================================
102. PR CAMPAIGN MODE
================================================================

Optional:

LOCAL_ONLY
DRAFT_PR
PR
NO_AUTO_MERGE

================================================================
103. NO AUTO-MERGE DEFAULT
================================================================

Fleet maintenance must not mass-merge by default.

================================================================
104. BLAST RADIUS
================================================================

Campaign has:

max_repositories
max_concurrent_mutations
max_PRs
max_failures

================================================================
105. FAILURE CIRCUIT BREAKER
================================================================

If campaign failure rate exceeds threshold:

pause campaign.

================================================================
106. SECURITY CIRCUIT BREAKER
================================================================

Any critical security invariant violation can immediately pause campaign.

================================================================
107. QUALITY CIRCUIT BREAKER
================================================================

Repeated regressions may pause campaign.

================================================================
108. COST CIRCUIT BREAKER
================================================================

For no-cost profile:

paid transport call attempt = hard stop.

================================================================
109. CAMPAIGN ROLLOUT
================================================================

Support:

CANARY
BATCHED
ALL

Default for large portfolio:

CANARY or bounded batch.

================================================================
110. CANARY
================================================================

Run small repository subset first.

Evaluate:

success
validation
security
repair attempts

Then proceed.

================================================================
111. CANARY PROMOTION
================================================================

Operator/policy can promote campaign to next batch.

================================================================
112. AUTOMATIC PROMOTION
================================================================

Allowed only under explicit rules.

Never based solely on model self-assessment.

================================================================
113. BATCH SIZE
================================================================

Configurable.

================================================================
114. CAMPAIGN ROLLBACK
================================================================

Do not promise automatic cross-repo rollback.

For local unpushed commits, cleanup/revert is possible.

For already-merged changes, separate remediation campaign may be
required.

Document truthfully.

================================================================
115. CAMPAIGN CHECKPOINTS
================================================================

Persist:

selected repos
completed
failed
running
next batch
policy version

================================================================
116. PORTFOLIO EVENTS
================================================================

Events:

CAMPAIGN_CREATED
CAMPAIGN_STARTED
REPO_TASK_CREATED
REPO_TASK_SUCCEEDED
REPO_TASK_FAILED
CAMPAIGN_PAUSED
CAMPAIGN_COMPLETED

================================================================
117. DURABLE CAMPAIGN OUTBOX
================================================================

Any remote mutation still uses EngineeringOperation journal.

No campaign-specific bypass.

================================================================
118. OPERATION RECONCILIATION
================================================================

Fleet restart:

reconcile UNKNOWN push/PR operations before dispatching retry.

================================================================
119. PORTFOLIO RESTART
================================================================

Kill fleet coordinator.

Restart.

Campaign progress remains.

No duplicate tasks.

================================================================
120. CAMPAIGN TASK IDEMPOTENCY
================================================================

Stable key:

campaign
repository
task template/version

prevents duplicate task creation.

================================================================
121. SCHEDULER RESTART
================================================================

Scheduler can rebuild queues from durable runnable task state.

Queue itself need not be persisted separately if safely reconstructable.

================================================================
122. NO RAM-ONLY SOURCE OF TRUTH
================================================================

Critical fleet state must remain reconstructable from durable storage.

================================================================
123. PORTFOLIO API
================================================================

Expose authorized API for:

repositories
health
campaigns
tasks
workers
fleet status

