## 36. Final Verdict

Never call simulated restart a hard-crash durability proof.

Never claim distributed fleet from a PostgreSQL adapter that was not
executed against real PostgreSQL.

Never claim REAL_GIT_ENGINEERING without actual git CLI worktree,
validation, commit and remote evidence.

Never retry UNKNOWN external mutations blindly.

Never allow a campaign to amplify an unsafe operation across dozens of
repositories.

Never optimize throughput ahead of security, quality, tenant isolation
or zero-paid policy.

Upgrade-22 succeeds when ZCoder can reliably coordinate autonomous
engineering across many repositories while surviving coordinator and
worker failures without duplicate engineering work or uncontrolled
remote mutations.